{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3.11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++14 code to Python 3.11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++14 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<bits/stdc++.h>\r\nusing namespace std;\r\n#define int long long\r\nconst int mod1=998244353;\r\nconst int mod2=1e9+7;\r\nint ans;\r\nint n;\r\nint cnt1;\r\nvector<int> val[7];\r\nint sum[7];\r\nvoid dfs1(int k1,int k2){\r\n\tif(k1==7)return;\r\n\tval[k1].push_back((cnt1-k2+mod1)%mod1);\r\n\tsum[k1]+=(cnt1-k2+mod1)%mod1;\r\n\tcnt1++;\r\n\tfor(int i=0;i<=9;++i){\r\n\t\tdfs1(k1+1,k2*10+i);\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\nbool check(int x){\r\n\tconst int half=1000000;\r\n\treturn x*half+999999<=n&&x*half*10>n;\r\n}\r\nint cnt2;\r\nint poww[7]={1,10,100,1000,10000,100000,1000000};\r\nvoid dfs2(int k1,int k2){\r\n\tif(k2>n)return;\r\n\tif(check(k2)){\r\n\t\tfor(int i=0;i<=6;++i){\r\n\t\t\tint offset=((cnt2+1-(k2*poww[i]))%mod1+mod1)%mod1;\r\n\t\t\tint pos=lower_bound(val[i].begin(),val[i].end(),mod1-offset)-val[i].begin();\r\n\t\t\t(ans+=(sum[i]+offset*val[i].size()-mod1*(val[i].size()-pos)))%=mod2;\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tcnt2+=cnt1;\r\n\t}\r\n\telse {\r\n\t\tcnt2++;\r\n\t\t(ans+=((cnt2-k2)%mod1+mod1)%mod1)%=mod2;\r\n\t\tfor(int i=(!k1);i<=9;++i){\r\n\t\t\tdfs2(k1+1,k2*10+i);\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\nsigned main(){\r\n\tscanf(\"%lld\",&n);\r\n\tdfs1(0,0);\r\n\tfor(int i=0;i<=6;++i)sort(val[i].begin(),val[i].end());\r\n\tcnt2=-1;\r\n\tdfs2(0,0);\r\n\tprintf(\"%lld\\n\",ans);\r\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "openai/gpt-4.1-nano"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nn = int(input())\n\nmod1 = 998244353\nmod2 = 10**9 + 7\n\nans = 0\ncnt1 = 0\nval = [[] for _ in range(7)]\nsum_arr = [0] * 7\n\ndef dfs1(k1, k2):\n    global cnt1\n    if k1 == 7:\n        return\n    val[k1].append((cnt1 - k2) % mod1)\n    sum_arr[k1] += (cnt1 - k2) % mod1\n    cnt1 += 1\n    for i in range(10):\n        dfs1(k1 + 1, k2 * 10 + i)\n\ndef check(x):\n    half = 10**6\n    return x * half + 999999 <= n and x * half * 10 > n\n\ncnt2 = 0\npoww = [1, 10, 100, 1000, 10000, 100000, 1000000]\n\ndef dfs2(k1, k2):\n    global ans, cnt2\n    if k2 > n:\n        return\n    if check(k2):\n        for i in range(7):\n            offset = ((cnt2 + 1 - (k2 * poww[i])) % mod1 + mod1) % mod1\n            # Binary search for position\n            import bisect\n            pos = bisect.bisect_left(val[i], mod1 - offset)\n            ans += (sum_arr[i] + offset * len(val[i]) - mod1 * (len(val[i]) - pos)) % mod2\n        cnt2 += cnt1\n    else:\n        cnt2 += 1\n        ans = (ans + ((cnt2 - k2) % mod1 + mod1) % mod1) % mod2\n        for i in range(0 if k1 == 0 else 1, 10):\n            dfs2(k1 + 1, k2 * 10 + i)\n\n# Perform the computations\ndfs1(0, 0)\nfor i in range(7):\n    val[i].sort()\ncnt2 = -1\ndfs2(0, 0)\n\nprint(ans)\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0013276183744892478, -0.00021212305000517517, -4.320199877838604e-07, -7.994086627149954e-05, -0.08324740827083588, -0.11283667385578156, -6.704273118884885e-07, -1.9361264946837764e-07, -0.10175309330224991, -0.09056804329156876, -4.320199877838604e-07, -0.004123753868043423, 0.0, 0.0, -1.9361264946837764e-07, -1.3856492842023727e-0